      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0276",
      "sequence": 288,
      "meaning": "Lakṣmaṇa says, ‘Sage, who in the world does not know your character? You repaid your debt to mother and father very thoroughly, but a great worry remained in your heart: your debt to your guru. It seems he charged that debt to my account; many days have passed and the interest has grown large. Call the accountant-creditor now, and I will immediately open my purse and pay.’ Hearing these cutting words, Paraśurāma raises his axe as the whole assembly cries out in alarm. Lakṣmaṇa continues: ‘Best of Bhṛgus, show me your axe! I spare you as a Brahmin, enemy of kings. You have never met fierce champions in battle; Brahmin deities grow powerful only at home.’ Everyone cries that this is improper. With a gesture Raghupati restrains Lakṣmaṇa. Seeing Lakṣmaṇa’s answers feed Bhṛgu’s fire of anger like oblations, the sun of Raghu speaks cooling words like water.",
